WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.660
There are few situations
more dangerous than

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.610
entering a burning
building. Thermoplastic

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.920
fire helmets weigh
substantially less than

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.210
other alternatives.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.610
These helmets are one
piece of equipment that

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.710
won't slow down the
rescue mission.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.230
Production starts with
the special blend of

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.850
thermoplastic pellets.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.730
A vacuum pulls the
pellets into a hopper.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.340
The pellets then flow
into an injection molding

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.250
machine. It melts and
molds the pellets into

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.270
the shape of a fire
helmet.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.320
A robot retrieves the
helmet and transfers it

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.730
to a cooling station.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.600
A worker then clips off
plastic that solidified

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.550
as it flowed through a
channel and into the

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.970
mold. This unwanted bit
is called sprue.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.480
She wipes off
fingerprints and inspects

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.130
the condition of the
helmet shell.

